            "review_title": "Review at Hoang Thi Cafe",
            "review_text": "Theo\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam78 contributions\n1\nA Cup of Old Saigon\nMar 2020\nTo say the Vietnamese love their coffee is an understatement. Second to phở, I think coffee is the second most consumed item in Vietnam. From megachains to small mom and pop shops there are thousands of coffee houses in Saigon. And their favored way drinking it has to be cà phê sữa đá, or drip coffee served with sweetened condensed milk served over ice.\n\nMy favorite cà phê sữa đá in all of Saigon has to be at Hoang Thi Cafe just a short 5 minute walk from Ben Thanh Market. Not only do I get a delicious glass of iced coffee but I also get to step back into time to 1950s Saigon. The cafe is decorated with authentic vintage furniture and furnishings. I feel like a character from Graham Greene’s “The Quiet American,” every time I visit.\n\nThe staff speak English and are absolutely charming and delightful. I hear that the owner is also an accomplished áo dài (traditional Vietnamese dress) designer that has done costumes for movies and television shows, and you can see a small collection of her beautiful dresses at the cafe. \n\nIf you visit Ben Thanh Market (and you will) make a small detour and experience a bit of Saigon’s past and stop by Hoang Thi Cafe. A real must to get the full Vietnam experience when visiting Saigon.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 9, 2020",
